            <ArticleTitle>[Homocystein and cardiovascular risk: is dosage useful?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2093-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hyperhomocysteinemia represents an independent risk factor for atherothrombotic disease. Physiopathological mechanisms of accelerated progression of atherosclerosis in presence of hyperhomocysteinemia are complex. Herein we report a clinical case which emphasis the importance of screening elevated homocystein in the absence of conventional risk factors in patients who suffer from premature atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
